@startuml
title Bounded AI Research Investigation

actor User
participant "AI settings" as SettingsUI
participant "Investigation panel" as UI
participant "AI research routes" as API
participant "AgentCloak Desktop setup\n(Vision service)" as Setup
participant "Investigation service\n(serial queue)" as Orchestrator
participant "Reference service\n(scoped local restoration)" as References
participant "AgentCloak preflight\n(Vision service)" as Preflight
participant "AgentCloak endpoint\n(Desktop /detect or MCP /mcp)" as AgentCloak
database "PostgreSQL\njobs, passages, disclosure metadata,\nencrypted reference maps" as DB
participant "Bounded typed tools" as Tools
participant "Restricted analysis runtime" as Analysis
participant "Local Ollama" as Ollama
participant "Egress helper\n(short-lived process)" as Egress
participant "OpenAI Responses API" as OpenAI
collections "Private runtime env\n(reference key, provider config)" as Env

opt User enables AgentCloak Desktop in AI settings
  SettingsUI -> API: GET /agentcloak-desktop\nread effective state and fresh probe
  API -> Setup: Probe /detect and read preference
  Setup -> AgentCloak: Bounded loopback detection probe
  Setup --> API: enabled, available, mappingKeyConfigured, openAiEnabled
  API --> SettingsUI: Status without secrets
  SettingsUI -> API: PUT /agentcloak-desktop {enabled:true}
  API -> Setup: Probe then ensure reference key
  Setup -> AgentCloak: Bounded loopback detection probe
  Setup -> Env: Fill missing or blank key; preserve nonblank invalid key
  Setup -> DB: Save enabled boolean only
  Setup --> API: Updated status without secrets
  API --> SettingsUI: Status response
end

User -> UI: Select scope, depth, language,\nresearch mode, route, and approved API model
opt Selected summary or evidence contains explicit private literals
  User -> UI: Wrap literals as\n[[vision-ref:type|value]]
end
UI -> API: POST /disclosures/preview\nwith full investigation request
opt Selected text has markers or Desktop mode is enabled
  API -> References: Parse supported typed markers
  opt Desktop mode
    References -> Preflight: Detect selected-summary and evidence spans\nwith token identifiers masked
    Preflight -> AgentCloak: POST /detect over loopback
    AgentCloak --> Preflight: Validated spans or block
    References -> References: Replace findings with scoped subject tokens
  end
  References -> References: Create scope UUID and\n18-byte CSPRNG tokens
  opt Markers or detections created tokens
    References -> DB: Store 15-minute unclaimed scope +\nAES-256-GCM ciphertext, nonce, and tag
  end
  References --> API: Tokenized outboundRequest +\nscope id, expiry, and count
end
opt AgentCloak preflight enabled
  API -> Preflight: Present user-authored cloud fields\nafter Vision tokenization
  alt Desktop mode
    Preflight -> AgentCloak: POST /detect with token identifiers masked
    AgentCloak --> Preflight: No spans or remaining finding
  else MCP mode
    Preflight -> AgentCloak: MCP cloak with token identifiers replaced by REFERENCE
    AgentCloak --> Preflight: Unchanged text or proposed change
  end
  alt Finding, changed text, unavailable, or invalid response
    Preflight --> API: Block cloud preview
  end
end
API --> UI: Exact tokenized payload, digest,\nreference warning, and preflight status
UI -> API: POST /investigations\nwith preview outboundRequest
API -> Orchestrator: Strict typed request
Orchestrator -> DB: Persist queued job
opt Request has a reference scope
  Orchestrator -> References: Validate every token; claim scope
  References -> DB: Bind scope atomically to one job;\nset 30-day expiry
end
alt Material ambiguity
  Orchestrator -> DB: Persist waiting plan
  UI --> User: Request clarification and typed date scope
else Scope is sufficient
  alt Selected-evidence cloud synthesis
    User -> UI: Enter exact task and evidence
    User -> UI: Inspect exact synthesis payload
    UI -> API: Create dedicated digest-bound grant
    API -> DB: Create digest-bound grant
    Orchestrator -> DB: Checkpoint selected evidence
  else Local planning
    Orchestrator -> Ollama: Candidate step identifiers
    Ollama --> Orchestrator: Prioritized identifiers
  else Opt-in OpenAI planning
    User -> UI: Inspect exact outbound planning payload
    UI -> API: Create digest-bound grant
    API -> DB: Create digest-bound grant
    opt AgentCloak preflight enabled, for each send attempt
      Orchestrator -> Preflight: Check canonical user-authored cloud text
      Preflight -> AgentCloak: Desktop /detect or MCP cloak on token-safe text
      AgentCloak --> Preflight: Clean or block; no payload rewrite
    end
    Orchestrator -> DB: Reserve disclosure and spend budgets
    Orchestrator -> Egress: Canonical allowlisted planning payload\nwith selected model and its price
    Egress -> OpenAI: POST /v1/responses\nstore=false, tools=[]
    OpenAI --> Egress: Prioritized identifiers, catalog plans, and usage
    Egress --> Orchestrator: Bounded response
  end
  Orchestrator -> DB: Persist constrained plan
end
alt Selected-evidence cloud synthesis
  opt AgentCloak preflight enabled, for each send attempt
    Orchestrator -> Preflight: Check canonical selected evidence
    Preflight -> AgentCloak: Desktop /detect or MCP cloak on token-safe text
    AgentCloak --> Preflight: Clean or block; no payload rewrite
  end
  Orchestrator -> DB: Reserve disclosure and spend budgets
  Orchestrator -> Egress: Canonical selected-evidence payload\nwith selected model and its price
  Egress -> OpenAI: POST /v1/responses\nstore=false, tools=[]
  OpenAI --> Egress: Structured final answer and usage
  Egress --> Orchestrator: Bounded response
else Local evidence workflow
  loop Each incomplete step
    alt Cloud-authored catalog analysis step
      Orchestrator -> Analysis: Validate catalog and workspace; inject trusted scope
      Analysis --> Orchestrator: Private local rows or explicit failure
    else Locally authored tool step
      Orchestrator -> Tools: Dispatch allowlisted tool with caps
      Tools --> Orchestrator: Evidence or explicit partial failure
    end
    Orchestrator -> DB: Checkpoint step result
  end

  opt Detailed mode has failed local steps
    Orchestrator -> Ollama: Inspect partial evidence and failed local candidates
    Ollama --> Orchestrator: Select up to three retry identifiers
    Orchestrator -> Tools: One serial local retry pass
    Orchestrator -> DB: Checkpoint revised plan and retry results
  end

  Orchestrator -> Ollama: Selected local evidence only
  Ollama --> Orchestrator: Structured answer candidate
end

Orchestrator -> DB: Persist validated provider-form answer\nin checkpoint_json before restoration
Orchestrator -> References: Restore only allowlisted answer text
References -> DB: Load same-job encrypted map
References -> References: Authenticate and decrypt with\ninstallation-held key
alt Unknown, malformed, expired, cross-job, or undecryptable token
  References --> Orchestrator: Explicit restoration failure
  Orchestrator -> DB: Mark job failed; do not expose\npartly restored provider answer
else Safe local answer
  References --> Orchestrator: Locally restored display text
end
Orchestrator -> Orchestrator: Validate citations and answer schema
Orchestrator -> DB: Complete, partial, failed, or cancelled
API --> UI: Facts, calculations, interpretations,\ngaps, conflicts, and evidence
UI --> User: Inspectable evidence-backed answer

note right of Orchestrator
One active job bounds CPU and RAM.
External checkpoints are never replayed by the retry loop.
No automatic cloud fallback.
Financial calculations use deterministic services.
Cloud synthesis receives only manually selected evidence.
Cloud planning receives identifiers, never relations, SQL, private scope IDs, or rows.
Cloud-authored analysis rows remain private and are synthesized locally.
Selected models come from the server allowlist.
Per-model prices drive spend reservation.
Explicit markers become typed one-job tokens; this is pseudonymization, not anonymity.
Optional Desktop detection protects selected text before preview and blocks remaining findings.
The MCP option blocks changed or unverified text. Vision performs local restoration.
It never rewrites the digest-bound OpenAI payload. Local chat is untouched.
The AES-256-GCM key is installation state outside PostgreSQL and database backup.
Restart validates the provider-form checkpoint and restores locally without another model call.
Job deletion cascades to its claimed scope and encrypted entries.
end note

@enduml
